User Journey Map

Stage 1: Receiving Money

Actions: - Receives allowance, scholarship funds, or income from a side hustle.
Thoughts & Feelings: - Relief at receiving money - Awareness that the money must last
Pain Points: - No clear plan for daily spending

Stage 2: Planning & Budgeting

Actions: - Mentally plans expenses or divides money into categories - Sets aside money for saving or investing
Thoughts & Feelings: - Wants to be disciplined - Unsure if the budget is realistic
Pain Points: - Manual tracking is easy to forget - No automatic feedback

Stage 3: Daily Spending Decisions

Actions: - Spends on food and transport - Considers whether purchases are necessary
Thoughts & Feelings: - Guilt when spending - Constant calculation in the head
Pain Points: - Doesn’t know exact remaining daily limit - Temptation to overspend

Stage 4: Overspending Risk

Actions: - Makes unplanned purchases - Realizes money is running out faster than expected
Thoughts & Feelings: - Stress and regret - Fear of not making it through the week
Pain Points: - No system to stop overspending

Stage 5: Desired App Experience

Actions: - App shows daily safe-to-spend amount - App automatically adjusts limits - App blocks spending after weekly limit
Thoughts & Feelings: - Sense of control - Reduced guilt - Confidence in financial decisions
Opportunities: - Offline functionality - Simple, ad-free interface - Strong spending limits and alerts.


