2. Nkhomotabo: The Friction-Averse, Reward-Oriented Spender
Quote: "I just freestyle... I know my balance, so I know if I'm spending this much money... I deserve to reward myself just a little bit with ice cream."

Nkhomotabo is a student who receives a large stipend once per trimester, making long-term planning essential but difficult. They are highly friction-averse, stating they would delete the app if it required "a lot of documentation, writing, filling out forms." They use a "freestyle" mental budget, which often leads to the sudden, stressful realization of being broke. Nkhomotabo balances paying fixed bills with justifying small, frequent "rewards" like ice cream. Their need is for an effortless, simple system that provides proactive, real-time alerts to manage their large, infrequent income without the stress of manual data entry.

