3. Tapiwanashe: The Cash-Conscious Planner
Quote: "I just look at the bundle of cash. Like, is it getting less and less smaller? If I see that the bundle is too big... I just spend. But if I see that it is getting smaller... I have to buy food that is cheaper."

Tapiwanashe is a student whose budgeting is heavily reliant on physical, visual cues—specifically, the size of his cash bundle. He uses mental "guesswork" to manage his monthly allowance, which he often withdraws as cash. His primary pain point is the tediousness of manual data entry for cash transactions, which he finds "boring" and leads to inaccurate tracking. He is a planner at heart, thinking about whether a purchase is "worth it" compared to cooking, but he lacks a reliable, low-friction tool to support his planning. He needs a system that can seamlessly integrate his cash spending into a dynamic, daily "safe-to-spend" limit.

