4. Veronica: The Impromptu Spender with Security Concerns
Quote: "If it's slow, if I press buttons and they are unresponsive, if I have a lot of ads... you guys are selling my information. Maybe locking down my savings so that I don't enjoy it."

Veronica is a student who earns income from online side jobs and is actively trying to transition from "impromptu" spending to disciplined saving. Her concerns are centered on trust, performance, and self-sabotage. She views intrusive ads and slow performance as red flags that indicate a lack of respect for her data and time. She needs a high-performance, privacy-focused application that offers features to help her overcome her own lack of discipline, such as a "savings lock" to prevent her from dipping into reserved funds. She is looking for a personalized tool that offers tangible benefits beyond a simple digital ledger.

